There is something important being missed by most of the people in
this discussion. I don't say this to diss you, Kent, because but for
one game I'm in the same boat: you have never ascended.  You are
thoroughly spoiled and have knowledge of what the game holds in all
its phases, but for whatever reason you have never ascended, and
presumably don't hit the planes, or the ascent with the amulet, or
perhaps even the ritual all that often.

So vanilla is still *interesting* for you (and me). You haven't
ascended so many times that seeing the Sanctum isn't even that
interesting. Your adrenaline still rushes right after you kill Rodney,
because you know the game has to go FAST from there. You get scared
and excited during a titan's summoning storm, because you know more
than likely it will kill you, no problem.

As I say, I'm in the same boat.

Most of the people participating in this discussion -- certainly
Derek, who is doing the Sporkhack development -- aren't in this
position anymore.  For them, beating the Castle is the *end* of the
interesting part of the game. (Derek said as much.) And so they feel
vanilla is broken, or at least uninteresting, because they can beat it
readily.

When you're like us, and ascension is never a sure thing no matter
what stage you reach, it's more important emotionally to get to the
parts you haven't beaten -- or have beaten less frequently. And so the
impermanence of Sporkhack armor becomes a genuine pain in the ass.
It's not restoring excitement, it's GETTING IN YOUR WAY of getting to
the exciting parts of Nethack you're not overly familiar with.

I'm putting words in everyone's mouth and I know that's a sin, so I
apologize herewith. But I think I'm not 100% wrong.



